  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 26046,
  "published": "2026-08-04T11:49:23.86Z",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.0.2: Restore per-environment fallback for DATA connections\n\t\t\t- MetadataConnectionResolver: sentinels (metadata + identity) stay strict exact-match, but\n\t\t\t  data connections (e.g. TAB_Core / app connections) again fall back to the environment's\n\t\t\t  registered connection on an exact-id miss. This restores per-environment routing (TAB-core\n\t\t\t  tables -> PMS_DEV / PMS_QA etc.) that v1.0.1 removed too broadly, which broke queries in any\n\t\t\t  non-platform environment. The loud-failure safety is kept only for the two sentinels.\n\n\t\t\tv1.0.1: Identity DB split support\n\t\t\t- Added IDENTITY_CONNECTION_ID sentinel (routes Identity-owned AppObjects to TAF.Identity,\n\t\t\t  forced to the TAF platform environment, exact-match — env-independent like the metadata sentinel)\n\t\t\t- MetadataConnectionResolver: removed the silent FirstOrDefault fallback for data connections;\n\t\t\t  a connection-id miss now returns null (caller throws) instead of routing to an arbitrary DB\n\n\t\t\tv1.0.0: Initial release\n\t\t\t- Moved connection resolution infrastructure from CRUD Service\n\t\t\t- Added IConnectionMetadataProvider abstraction for flexible metadata sources\n\t\t\t- ConfigConnectionResolver: Resolves from appsettings.json\n\t\t\t- MetadataConnectionResolver: Resolves from metadata provider with 5-minute caching\n\t\t\t- ConnectionResolverFactory: Config-driven resolver selection\n\t\t\t- ConnectionHelper: Connection string building utilities\n\t\t\t- ResolvedConnection: Pre-built connection string wrapper\n\t\t\t- Supports SQL Server and PostgreSQL",
